sam-sales: Quick sync: AuroraCard wants a short POC next week. Requirements: streaming UX + final structured JSON that conforms to their transaction schema, function/tool-calling for account lookups, SAML SSO later, and IP allowlist during the trial. Also asked for a ballpark dedicated commit for 3 A100 equiv nodes.

leo-se: Got it. Short plan: demo on hosted with streaming SSE to show latency, implement a function_call pattern to return the canonical JSON, then validate server-side before handing to their pipeline.

sam-sales: They specifically want token-level streaming in the UI while still guaranteeing the final JSON is syntactically valid and matches field types.

nina-presales: Recommendation: stream deltas for UX, but treat the function_call as the truth. On function_call event send the full args payload and run JSON Schema validation. For resilience, return an error schema if validation fails so their integrators can surface errors.

leo-se: Tiny JS snippet we can share with their eng team (uses our JS SDK and SSE):
```js
const resp = await client.chat.stream({ model: 'redwood/stream-lite', messages, functions });
resp.on('delta', (d) => ui.appendToken(d.text));
resp.on('function_call', (f) => {
  // f.arguments is a JSON string with the final structured payload
  const payload = JSON.parse(f.arguments);
  const ok = validateSchema(payload);
  if (!ok) sendValidationError(payload);
  else persistToQueue(payload);
});
```

sam-sales: Perfect. Any PII considerations for streaming? They may have partial account ids in prompts.

nina-presales: For PII we recommend masking in the UI and only sending minimal identifiers in requests. Also enable token redaction in logs and set short retention for telemetry during POC.

leo-se: About SAML + IP allowlist: for the PoC we can do the hosted flow with IP allowlist (we need their static egress IPs). For full SAML-backed access and VPC isolation they'd be on Private or Dedicated. Dedicated onboarding is roughly 2-3 weeks after PO and SSO metadata.

sam-sales: Pricing ask: what should I tell them for 3x A100 committed monthly?

nina-presales: Ballpark range is between "$XX,XXX" and "$YY,YYY" / month depending on retention, burst policy, and support tier. I'll fetch exact quote from finance. Offer: trial credits on hosted first to validate integration.

leo-se: Operational items to prep for the eng runbook: 1) sample SDK streaming code (above), 2) how to detect and parse function_call event, 3) schema validation example and error payloads, 4) IP allowlist steps (what IPs we need, how to rotate keys), 5) telemetry headers to correlate traces.

sam-sales: Can someone prepare a 1-page runbook and a short checklist for the SREs? They asked for trace + cost per route visibility.

nina-presales: I'll draft the runbook and include: minimal SDK snippets (JS + Python), expected timelines, POC constraints, and a pricing stub. Aim to share in 3 hours.

infra-bot: NOTE: Dedicated onboarding checklist: signed contract, SSO metadata, infra diagram, billing contact. Estimated 2-3 weeks.

leo-se: Also: if they want prefix caching / KV for repeated lookups during streaming, use ephemeral session keys to avoid leaking cross-session state and to reduce token consumption.

sam-sales: Okay. Action items: Nina will draft runbook + price ballpark; Leo will prepare a tiny validation lambda and telemetry header sample; I'll ask the customer for static egress IPs and their JSON schema or sample outputs. If we don't get full schema in 24h we'll mock using the CSV.

nina-presales: Added: include recommended function schema for the model (fields, types, required list) so we reduce iteration.

sam-sales: Thanks all. Will update after kickoff. :rocket:
